                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "While I understand some of the critique, I still think this is a nice addition to the series, addressing both the needlessly expansive game world and a great deal of jank revolving around the potato gun by completely nixing it entirely. Do I miss the complete lack of puzzle solving? Sure, but it still maintains the wonderfully bizarre atmosphere of the original [i]Sylvio[/i], Maia reprises her role as Juliette, and personally, cool as the reel-to-reel deck was, I think the haunted audio spectrums and video analysis are decent enough novelties in their own right.\n\nThe real gem, though, is traveling via the rusty trawler. An entire game where you explore a post-apocalypse of cosmic horrors by boat, decorated in occult artifacts—akin to the statues here—would be absolutely brilliant and I would quite frankly play the shit out of that if it existed.\n\nDefinitely don't let the negative reviews scare you; if you enjoyed [i]Sylvio[/i], but wished it had been better structured, you're doing a disservice to yourself by skipping its sequel.",
